{"actor":"Stephanie Schofield","comment":null,"created_at":"2026-03-08T23:09:51Z","event_type":"claimed","id":28,"issue_id":"beth-cip.1","new_value":"{\"assignee\":\"Stephanie Schofield\",\"status\":\"in_progress\"}","old_value":"{\"id\":\"beth-cip.1\",\"title\":\"Dependency enforcement on bd close\",\"description\":\"Make bd close respect the dependency graph as a hard gate, not advisory. When closing an issue: 1) Check all --deps are in closed status. 2) Check all child test subtasks are closed (quality gate integration). 3) If any blocking deps are still open, refuse to close and print what's blocking. Example: 'bd close beth-gtl.3' fails with 'Cannot close — beth-gtl.2 (open) still blocking.' This is the lowest-cost, highest-value enforcement. The dependency data already exists in dolt — just needs a check in the close path. Could be implemented as a bd plugin/hook or as a wrapper script in the beth project.\",\"status\":\"open\",\"priority\":1,\"issue_type\":\"task\",\"owner\":\"sschofield@microsoft.com\",\"created_at\":\"2026-03-07T18:47:37Z\",\"created_by\":\"Stephanie Schofield\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-03-07T18:47:37Z\"}"}
